// 01 - Hello, Thunder!
//
// The smallest useful program. Statements at the top level of a file run
// from top to bottom, one statement per line. println writes its arguments
// followed by a newline.
//
// Try it: press Compile and look at the Tokens tab. The lexer has split the
// text into an identifier (println), punctuation and a string literal.
// Notice that the end of a line ends the statement: no separator is needed.

println("Hello, Thunder!")
println("Welcome to Programming Language Technology.")
